  "facts": [
    "Reflect downcasts require exact Any type identity. ReflectDeserialize::FromType<T> calls T::deserialize, so this entry preserves the selected concrete type's Serde admission; it is not generic proof of raw-field construction or a separate schema.",
    "Saphyr from_str and options entry points both call T::deserialize with selected options. Default rejects nonfinite typeless float, but documented concrete float handling remains independent: this policy must not be mistaken for concrete f32/f64 validation. Duplicate-key error/merge policy and strict boolean defaults are distinct parser policies, not bespoke invariant authority."
